Bandgap + constant-swing reference over PVT (operating point)
* iout0 into 0.7 V (a block's NMOS diode level): reference current; iout1 into a high_po resistor of the
* CML-load type (6 kOhm): I * R, the swing proxy that should not move with the resistor corner.
.lib "@MODEL_LIBRARY@" @SECTION@
.include "@PROJECT_ROOT@/analog/common/devices/spice/sky130_primitives.spice"
.include "@PROJECT_ROOT@/analog/common/devices/spice/sky130_pfet_lvt.spice"
.include "@PROJECT_ROOT@/analog/common/bias/spice/bandgap.spice"
Vdd vdd 0 @SUPPLY@
Xbg vbg i0 i1 i2 i3 vg vgi vdd 0 serdes_bandgap
Vi0 i0 0 0.7
Xrl i1 0 0 sky130_fd_pr__res_high_po w=1 l=18
Vi2 i2 0 0.7
Vi3 i3 0 0.7
* operating-point guess for the multi-loop circuit (the physical state is checked by the power-up transient)
.nodeset v(vbg)=1.23 v(xbg.s)=1.23 v(vg)=0.9 v(vgi)=0.9 v(xbg.ta)=0.95 v(xbg.tb)=0.95
.temp @TEMP_C@
.options reltol=1e-5 abstol=1p vntol=1u klu
